<v Maya>Nothing at all. It proves the math is right, but it is a complete black box regarding how the math got there in the first place. Yeah. And that leaves us with some incredibly heavy, unresolved tensions for you to think about. I mean, we just witnessed... 88 hours of compute costing</v>

152
00:17:44.156 --> 00:17:49.579
<v Maya>millions of dollars, resulting in a mathematically perfect yet highly contested paper.</v>

153
00:17:49.659 --> 00:17:55.802
<v Daniel>And that raises a vital question about the future. What does this say about which open problems become tractable moving forward?</v>

154
00:17:55.862 --> 00:17:56.823
<v Maya>Oh, that's a great point.</v>

155
00:17:56.943 --> 00:18:11.931
<v Daniel>And more importantly, who holds the capital to afford to attack them? I mean, if finding the next breakthrough costs $5 million in server time and requires 10,000 coordinating agents, the independent researcher at a small university is entirely</v>

156
00:18:11.991 --> 00:18:12.911
<v Daniel>locked out of the game.</v>

157
00:18:13.091 --> 00:18:27.599
<v Maya>Exactly. For thousands of years, mathematics has been a slow, deeply human, collaborative pursuit of truth. But if discovering that truth now requires a multi-million dollar server farm chatting in the dark, does mathematics stop being a human</v>

158
00:18:27.639 --> 00:18:28.299
<v Maya>philosophy?</v>

159
00:18:28.900 --> 00:18:29.260
<v Daniel>It might.</v>

160
00:18:29.802 --> 00:18:42.241
<v Maya>Does it just become another industrial scale extraction industry entirely owned by a few tech monopolies? I mean, you wake up, you drink your coffee and the machine has already solved the universe, but it won't tell you whose ideas are borrowed to do it.</v>

161
00:18:42.742 --> 00:18:46.768
<v Daniel>It is a profound shift in how we define human knowledge itself.</v>

162
00:18:46.968 --> 00:18:53.338
<v Maya>It really is. Well, thank you for taking this deep dive with us. Keep questioning the source code and we'll catch you on the next one.</v>
